 "note": "The shift-15 window: same place as the old Scandinavia, 15 tiles south, with the zealand-funen feature overrides. Land 59.4-59.7% against the old window's 52.1-53.0%, IoU 0.847-0.848 (old: 0.833-0.855), 8 TCs at 49.7 walked separation (old: 47.9/40.0), one landmass fully reachable. Ships with zealand-funen rather than the full-sound variant, which reached N=10 and did not separate Zealand in 9 of 9 captures (bc0bc20) - the thing it existed to do. N=2 on this window so far; exclusive land min/median is 0.77 and 0.81 across those two, so the low end sits just under the 0.79-0.96 band stock maps hold.",
